    "created_at": "2017-10-02T11:47:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-02T11:47:55Z",
    "body": "> https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#intrinsic-dimensions suggests it probably does not.\r\n\r\nThat link states:\r\n\r\n> If an object (such as an icon) has multiple sizes, then the largest size (by area) is taken as its intrinsic size. If it has multiple aspect ratios at that size, or has multiple aspect ratios and no size, then the aspect ratio closest to the aspect ratio of the default object size is used.\r\n\r\nAnd the [HTML spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#the-video-element:default-object-size) says:\r\n\r\n> The default object size is a width of 300 CSS pixels and a height of 150 CSS pixels.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/333511600/reactions",
